Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

RED on 6f3dc7c (5 failures, evidence/A5b_red.txt): add_entity's merge
path did NOT increment revision, violating the documented contract
('every add/contradiction increments it' — the comment above the
field) and leaving delta_since blind to evidence accumulation on
existing entities (revision_to == revision_from for pure
re-observation). The merge path also replaced metadata wholesale with
the winner's — extras from the losing side were silently dropped.

Fix: the merge path increments revision; metadata merges additively —
methods_seen accumulates with set semantics (independent of the
provenance winner), status_code keeps the LATEST (current state),
identity facets carry the new observation's explicit values, all other
keys merge with new-wins-on-conflict so extras from either side
survive.

Contract suite (11): merge increments; monotonic across 4
observations; duplicate relation rejected WITHOUT moving the counter;
contradiction increments; refs dedup; first-observed-at stays oldest;
delta_since sees re-observation (revision_to > revision_from +
provenance_changes); stronger wins; weaker never downgrades; refs
capped at 50 on the merge path; metadata extras preserved.

GREEN: 11/11 (evidence/A5b_green.txt); A5a suite still green (23/23
combined).
